<h2>Segment 251 &mdash; humans perceive and use water</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s251S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w1">mi</span> <span class="u plural" data-d="6" data-l="s251p1">rnams</span> kyis ni <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w2">mngar ba</span> dang , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w3">dvangs pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p2">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w4">bsil ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w5">chur</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w6">rtogs</span> shing <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w7">&#x27;thung</span> ngo , , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w8">khrus byed</span> do, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w9">de<span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m1">r</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w10">&#x27;jug</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s251S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w1">Humans</span> look at the same thing and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w6">perceive</span> it as <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w5">water</span>--<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w2">sweet</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w3">clear</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p2">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w4">cool</span>. They <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w7">drink</span> of it, they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w8">wash</span> themselves with it, and they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w10">swim</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w9"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m1">in</span> it</span>.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p1"><span class="nul">Plurality is fused into Humans; no separate English plural word.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment proposed independently by Codex (gpt-6-astra), Tibetan-first. Mi is human here, not negation. Rnams has no separate word because plurality is fused into Humans. The selected dang is the second Tibetan occurrence, after dvangs pa, and owns and immediately before cool; the other English occurrences of and remain unwrapped. Chur retains its case ending intact; water is the lexical exponent, while as is the distributed predicative frame and is not forced into a member. Khrus byed is the established washing predicate; themselves with it is supplied. Der is the inflected demonstrative in it, with its unique r member aligned to in; 'jug is contextually swim. The earlier English look at the same thing is an explicating expansion of perception and context; rtogs is banked only once at perceive. The first dang, kyis, ni, the genitive, shing and clause endings are omitted; no unresolved relation is labelled null. Initial go of C05:252 closes this row's 'jug across the preserved row boundary (registered E-111 class); it is not moved or re-filed.</div>
